---
title: Lasagna
source: Aunt Julie
servings: 6
prep time: 30 minutes
cook time: 2 hours
---

= Sauce

In a #skillet{}, cook @ground turkey{1%lb}, @onion{0.75%cup}, and @minced
garlic{}. Drain the fat.

Add @petite diced tomatoes{1%lb}, @tomato sauce{15%oz}, @parsley{2%tbsp},
@sugar{2%tbsp}, @salt{1%tsp}, and @basil{1%tsp}. Heat to a boil then reduce
to a simmer. Simmer for ~{1%hour} then remove from heat.

= Cheese Mixture

In a #large bowl{}, combine @small curd cottage cheese{24%oz},
@parmesan{0.5%cup}, @parsley{1%tbsp}, and @oregano{1.5%tsp}.

= Assembly

Layer @oven ready lasagna noodles{1%box} onto the bottom of a #13x9 pan{}.

Add a layer of the cheese mixture, then some @mozzarella cheese{2%cups}. Add
sauce.

Repeat the layering 3 times, ending with sauce on top, then a final layer
of mozzarella.

Bake at 350 F for ~{50%minutes}.
